  "notes": [
    {
      "title": "index.ts is a monolith",
      "body": "server/index.ts (1991 LOC) inlines ~60 REST routes, the ws room and boot logic instead of splitting routers.",
      "severity": "warn",
      "path": "server/index.ts"
    },
    {
      "title": "actions.ts is the authority",
      "body": "Every producer (REST, ws, MCP, resident loop, linear/slack/github extensions) funnels through server/actions.ts \u2014 clean single mutation surface.",
      "severity": "info",
      "path": "server/actions.ts"
    },
    {
      "title": "memory + Postgres dual sources",
      "body": "state lives in server/store.ts Maps; db/persist.ts write-through mirrors each change. Crash-window gaps are patched at hydrate (orphaned frames rejoin page 1).",
      "severity": "info",
      "path": "server/db/persist.ts"
    },
    {
      "title": "resident loop is prompt-heavy",
      "body": "server/mcp.ts embeds a ~1k-word instruction prompt per tool call; workflow rules live with the model, not with the client.",
      "severity": "info",
      "path": "server/mcp.ts"
    },
    {
      "title": "model-tier fallback chain",
      "body": "server/resident.ts retries of the server tier then falls onto the requesting human's connected plan (chatgpt oauth, openai/openrouter/gemini/claude keys).",
